WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.360
TSMC is weighing a 20% co-OS price hike as packaging stays tight. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:12.760
Episode 39. After the packaging price, intel shifts client wafers toward data center CPUs,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:18.360
SK Heinix sends its memory chief to the United States, and two site fights show how neighbors

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:23.820
meet the build. Semiconductor Engineering's Weak &amp; Review is where that co-OS figure sits,

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.000
tied to AI demand still crowding advanced packaging.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.000
In the same review, ASC forecasts that its advanced packaging revenue doubles in 2027.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.480
AMCore, meanwhile, is ramping new high-density fan-out and new 2.5D programs.

00:00:39.576 --> 00:00:43.816
Intel is taking 18A wafers that had been headed for Panther Lake offline.

00:00:44.356 --> 00:00:49.456
Tom's hardware reports, so Oregon can run Intel 3 and build more granite rapids.

00:00:49.936 --> 00:00:54.776
Nova Lake, already on the client roadmap, is now the first 18AP client part.

00:00:54.776 --> 00:01:00.176
and Lip Bootan says it is tracking ahead of schedule. Design winds at launch are expected

00:01:00.176 --> 00:01:06.736
to be twice Panther lakes with more of the story at CES in January. Against 18A, 18A

00:01:06.736 --> 00:01:13.336
P is a 9% speed gain at the same power, or an 18% power cut at the same speed, and Intel

00:01:13.336 --> 00:01:19.016
has called it a drop-in. Wildcat Lake demand is already ahead of supply. The client business

00:01:19.016 --> 00:01:24.476
this is expected to fall more than 20 percent next quarter, and the 2026 PC unit market

00:01:24.476 --> 00:01:25.616
about 12 percent.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:31.692
SK Heinex has stood up a president-level America's organization in the United States and

00:01:31.692 --> 00:01:36.752
put development chief on Hionn in charge from November 1st, big-go finance reports.

00:01:37.292 --> 00:01:41.292
He has led AI memory work, including HBM and SOCAM.

00:01:41.792 --> 00:01:46.652
The job is a customer system aimed at U.S. big tech, plus a tighter hold on technology

00:01:46.652 --> 00:01:47.812
leadership and research.

00:01:48.452 --> 00:01:52.732
Chasun-Yong takes development and keeps the Future Technology Research Institute.

00:01:53.312 --> 00:01:58.312
Yoon-Pung-Yong moves to the Corporate Center, and Chief Executive Kwak No-Jong stays after

00:01:58.312 --> 00:01:59.912
six record quarters in a row.

00:02:01.038 --> 00:02:06.238
Han Mi-Semi-conductor said on October 30th that SK Heinex gave it a plaque for HBM tools

00:02:06.238 --> 00:02:09.178
and mass production support, Cho Sun-Biz reports.

00:02:09.878 --> 00:02:15.398
The link started with a 2015 thermal compression bonder, and equipment sales to SK Heinex over

00:02:15.398 --> 00:02:17.958
over 10 years come to about 600 billion won.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:23.998
In 2017, Han Mi built Korea's first dual thermal compression bonder, which it says roughly

00:02:23.998 --> 00:02:28.738
doubled productivity, and the pair shared the IR-52 Jang Young-Sill award.

00:02:29.338 --> 00:02:37.218
Those bonders have followed SK high-nicks from HBM2 through HBM3, HBM3E and HBM4, including

00:02:37.218 --> 00:02:38.538
memory supplied to Nvidia.

00:02:38.538 --> 00:02:38.698
India.

00:02:39.338 --> 00:02:44.818
Support sits in offices at Chongju and Ichon, plus a silver Phoenix team with 30 vehicles.

00:02:45.829 --> 00:02:51.669
Furiosa AI closed a $620 million series D to scale its data center inference accelerator

00:02:52.069 --> 00:02:53.569
and to push the next silicon.

00:02:54.349 --> 00:03:01.329
Named backers include Infinitum, Jericho Capital, QUAA Capital, Cisco Investments, Worldline

00:03:01.329 --> 00:03:05.449
Capital, Korea's National Growth Fund, and other Korean institutions.

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:07.989
HPC wire carried the clothes.

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:14.294
Brain Chips AKD 1500 Raspberry Pi 5 Kit is on sale now from the company's shop.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:21.694
A Raspberry Pi 5 plus the AKD 1500 M.2 card lets a team try the same chip it would design in,

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:24.134
over PCIe or SPI.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:27.594
Processing stays on the device, only events are handled,

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:31.234
and new classes can be learned on the chip without a cloud retrain.

00:03:31.974 --> 00:03:34.874
Meta-TF tools and models are free on the developer hub.

00:03:34.874 --> 00:03:41.865
C-SUN manufacturing set on October 30th that it will take 1,900 lots of NEMSTEC's private

00:03:41.865 --> 00:03:42.645
common shares.

00:03:43.125 --> 00:03:48.845
The expected holding is about 4.68%, and the point is more advanced packaging equipment.

00:03:49.877 --> 00:03:53.657
A 700-megawatt data center is announced outside Lansing, Michigan.

00:03:54.417 --> 00:03:59.357
Data Center Dynamics says local officials were blindsided by a proposal from the local economic

00:03:59.357 --> 00:04:00.517
development agency.

00:04:00.517 --> 00:04:07.137
SpaceX is reported by Tom's hardware to be buying 418 homes beside a flagship AI data

00:04:07.137 --> 00:04:12.517
center, and only from owners who quit a lawsuit. The houses are supposed to lodge SpaceX

00:04:12.517 --> 00:04:18.934
SI staff. They are also a way out for neighbors who do not want to live next to the site. Nordic

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:24.154
developer Hyme has taken an investment from Omniz. The money is for Hyme's first projects

00:04:24.154 --> 00:04:29.634
in Finland. Quantum DC's Australian project is announced at Gigawatt scale and already

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:34.394
has local pushback. The company called off a community meeting after what it described

00:04:34.394 --> 00:04:41.173
as a credible bomb threat. China's CXMT plans to start limited HBM3E production soon.

00:04:41.913 --> 00:04:47.433
Semiconductor engineering says, citing Reuters, yields are put at 20% to 30%.

00:04:47.433 --> 00:04:53.753
Vietnam's first semiconductor fab may miss a 2027 trial production target. Again, via Reuters

00:04:53.753 --> 00:04:59.953
in that review. The VietTel project is estimated at $1.3 billion and reportedly has

00:04:59.953 --> 00:05:04.753
not started construction. Talks for ASML lithography tools are still open.

00:05:05.493 --> 00:05:10.778
Viettel says the schedule still holds. Printed circuit board shortages are projected to

00:05:10.778 --> 00:05:16.918
run to 2030. Tech PowerUp reports from Nique Asia. An unnamed executive at an American

00:05:16.918 --> 00:05:22.698
PC maker said some suppliers do not expect orders placed today to land until late 2028.

00:05:23.498 --> 00:05:26.818
Boards are still short even if PC shipments fall again next year.

00:05:26.818 --> 00:05:33.281
Tanaka and MEP are setting up a precious metal refining joint venture in Batu-Kawan industrial

00:05:33.281 --> 00:05:34.101
park Penang.

00:05:34.921 --> 00:05:39.921
Tanaka takes 66.7% and MEP 33.3%.

00:05:39.921 --> 00:05:41.601
Semi-conductor digest reports.

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:43.021
Two shorter notes.

00:05:44.238 --> 00:05:49.678
IQM says its cloud emerald system has fully entangled all 54 qubits on the chip at once,

00:05:50.158 --> 00:05:52.558
with fidelity kept above the entanglement threshold.

00:05:53.358 --> 00:05:58.418
Atlanta's spin-out Nagari Labs raised $5 million from playground global for a new memory

00:05:58.418 --> 00:06:00.738
tier aimed at the AI memory bottleneck.

00:06:01.473 --> 00:06:04.693
A process node does not advance because the lab stays lit.

00:06:05.273 --> 00:06:09.813
Take it apart at the research clock, not the fab clock, and the distinction is the one

00:06:09.813 --> 00:06:13.993
YP Chine drew for students, as WCCF Tech reported.

00:06:14.613 --> 00:06:19.513
Production gains output when a second shift loads lots onto a tool that already has a qualified

00:06:19.513 --> 00:06:20.053
recipe.

00:06:20.893 --> 00:06:25.293
Lethography, etch, and deposition do not need the same engineer awake for every wafer.

00:06:25.793 --> 00:06:30.093
Development does because the next experiment is only useful after someone has read the

00:06:30.093 --> 00:06:30.793
last one.

00:06:31.253 --> 00:06:33.053
A wrong reading does not buy time.

00:06:33.373 --> 00:06:36.273
It buys another pile of wafers aimed at the wrong variable.

00:06:36.953 --> 00:06:41.153
Chine's point, as carried, is that research runs on brain power, not labor.

00:06:41.773 --> 00:06:46.933
Night owl is the worked case, from a stretch when TSMC was behind on process technology.

00:06:46.933 --> 00:06:52.513
The internal theory was that a research team on 24-hour days against U.S. competitors

00:06:52.513 --> 00:06:56.173
on 8-hour days would hold a time advantage and overtake them.

00:06:56.613 --> 00:07:02.413
24 divided by 8 is 3, so 3 times the staffed hours was supposed to mean 3 times the

00:07:02.413 --> 00:07:02.993
learning rate.

00:07:03.593 --> 00:07:07.553
Engineers were encouraged onto night development so the organization never closed.

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:11.513
The program was called a failure inside 6 months, half a year.

00:07:11.513 --> 00:07:17.373
The missing term was decision quality per hour, a tired team on a bad split converges on

00:07:17.373 --> 00:07:20.813
noise, and the morning shift spends the next day unwinding it.

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:25.413
That is why a three-fold hour's claim died in six months instead of compounding.

00:07:25.873 --> 00:07:30.993
Chine located the repair at the 40 nanometer node, where research used to finish a process

00:07:30.993 --> 00:07:32.333
and then hand it to the fab.

00:07:32.833 --> 00:07:34.773
That handoff hit serious setbacks.

00:07:35.313 --> 00:07:40.333
One team in his telling is shared ownership of the final result, not a plea to be helpful.

00:07:40.333 --> 00:07:45.953
He gave two examples, a longer overlap with the fab and development early, makes the ramp

00:07:45.953 --> 00:07:48.033
smoother when a process goes to volume.

00:07:48.633 --> 00:07:53.353
Several teams on a root cause clear a fab problem faster than one unit hunting it alone.

00:07:53.893 --> 00:07:55.673
He applies the same rule offshore.

00:07:56.393 --> 00:08:01.773
Fabs outside Taiwan cannot run fully cut off, and Taiwan teams have to carry part of the result.

00:08:02.213 --> 00:08:06.853
Getting departments to accept that shared accountability takes a long time, and slogans

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:07.653
do not do it.

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:11.953
The night shift becomes the right tool only when the recipe is already qualified.

00:08:12.393 --> 00:08:15.813
The split is already chosen, and metrology is already trusted.

00:08:16.493 --> 00:08:21.273
Night owl treated an open hypothesis as a loading problem, and the other 16 hours of

00:08:21.273 --> 00:08:25.733
the day could not finish a node whose next wafer still waited on an interpretation nobody

00:08:25.733 --> 00:08:26.253
had made.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:32.500
On the horizon, November 1st is the day on Hune's America's role at SK Heinex Takes Effect.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:37.940
January 2027 is when Intel expects to say more about Nova Lake at CES.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:45.020
Late 2028 is as soon as some boardmakers, Viennique, expect today's PCB orders to be filled,

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.480
with tightness projected toward 2030.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:55.920
Before we go, Vietel's claim that trial production still lands in 2027 is the date to test against a fab that has not broken ground.

